# Coding Conventions

## Naming

- Files: `snake_case.dart`
- Types/classes/enums: `PascalCase`
- Members/locals: `camelCase`
- Private: `_leadingUnderscore`
- Generated: do not hand-edit `*.g.dart` / `app_localizations*.dart`

## Money & ledger

- Store amounts as `int` minor units via `Money` — never `double` for balances
- `Money` arithmetic stays in one currency; convert with FX before combining currencies
- Writes go through `LedgerWriter.append` — append-only; corrections = new events
- Use `LedgerEventType` + `storageKey` for `eventType` column

## Flutter / Forui / Drift / Riverpod

- UI by feature under `lib/features/<feature>/` — prefer Forui widgets (`FScaffold`, `FHeader`, `FCard`, `FTile`, `FButton`, `FLucideIcons`)
- Root: `MaterialApp` + `FTheme` + `toApproximateMaterialTheme()` (see `lib/app.dart`)
- Schema tables under `lib/data/database/tables/`; bump `schemaVersion` + migration when changing tables
- After Drift/table changes: `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`
- After ARB changes: `flutter gen-l10n`
- User-facing strings: ARB only (`lib/l10n/app_en.arb`, `app_vi.arb`) — no hardcoded UI copy
- Prefer `ConsumerWidget` / `ConsumerStatefulWidget` for Riverpod

## Imports

Order: `dart:` → `package:` → relative.

## Comments

Explain why (append-only ledger, FX as-of date), not what the next line does.

## Commits

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `feat(capture): …`, `fix(ledger): …`, `refactor(money): …`, `test(ledger): …`, `chore: …`.

## Verify

```bash
flutter analyze
flutter test
```
